"}\n",[323,554,556],{"class":325,"line":555},17,[323,557,364],{"emptyLinePlaceholder":363},[323,559,561,564,567],{"class":325,"line":560},18,[323,562,563],{"class":329},"export",[323,565,566],{"class":329}," default",[323,568,569],{"class":340}," config\n",[229,571,572,573,576,577,580,581,583,584,587],{},"The CLI reads the first ",[252,574,575],{},"kinotic.config.*"," file it finds in ",[252,578,579],{},".config",", so a ",[252,582,531],{}," or ",[252,585,586],{},".json"," config\nis loaded the same way.",[589,590,592],"h4",{"id":591},"fields","Fields",[594,595,596,608],"table",{},[597,598,599],"thead",{},[600,601,602,606],"tr",{},[603,604,605],"th",{},"Field",[603,607,275],{},[609,610,611,625,637,653,669,683,717,732,744],"tbody",{},[600,612,613,619],{},[614,615,616],"td",{},[252,617,618],{},"organizationId",[614,620,621,624],{},[247,622,623],{},"Required."," The id of the Kinotic organization this project belongs to.",[600,626,627,632],{},[614,628,629],{},[252,630,631],{},"applicationId",[614,633,634,636],{},[247,635,623],{}," The application id this project belongs to. Must match the application id registered with Kinotic OS: lowercase letters, digits, and interior dashes.",[600,638,639,644],{},[614,640,641],{},[252,642,643],{},"projectId",[614,645,646,648,649,652],{},[247,647,623],{}," The id of this project in Kinotic OS. Provisioned repositories carry the id of the project that created them; ",[252,650,651],{},"kinotic sync"," addresses this project and fails when it does not exist.",[600,654,655,660],{},[614,656,657],{},[252,658,659],{},"name",[614,661,662,663,665,666,668],{},"Optional project name. When omitted, the ",[252,664,659],{}," from the project's ",[252,667,289],{}," is used.",[600,670,671,676],{},[614,672,673],{},[252,674,675],{},"description",[614,677,678,679,665,681,668],{},"Optional project description. When omitted, the ",[252,680,675],{},[252,682,289],{},[600,684,685,690],{},[614,686,687],{},[252,688,689],{},"entitiesPaths",[614,691,692,694,695,698,699,702,703,706,707,710,711,714,715,270],{},[247,693,623],{}," An array whose entries are either a plain path string or an ",[252,696,697],{},"EntitiesPathConfig"," object with ",[252,700,701],{},"path"," (the directory containing entity definitions), ",[252,704,705],{},"repositoryPath"," (where the CLI writes generated repository classes), and ",[252,708,709],{},"mirrorFolderStructure"," (whether to replicate the entity directory structure in the output, default ",[252,712,713],{},"true","). The CLI scans these paths when you run ",[252,716,651],{},[600,718,719,724],{},[614,720,721],{},[252,722,723],{},"generatedPath",[614,725,726,727,729,730,270],{},"The default output path for generated files, used for ",[252,728,689],{}," entries that are plain strings. Ignored for entries that use ",[252,731,697],{},[600,733,734,739],{},[614,735,736],{},[252,737,738],{},"fileExtensionForImports",[614,740,741,742,270],{},"The extension the CLI writes on import paths in generated code. Defaults to ",[252,743,531],{},[600,745,746,751],{},[614,747,748],{},[252,749,750],{},"validate",[614,752,753],{},"When true, generated repository classes validate data before sending it to the server.",[296,755,757],{"id":756},"project-dependencies","Project Dependencies",[229,759,760,761,763],{},"Projects within the same application can depend on each other. For example, a microservice project might import entity types defined in a persistence project. These dependencies are managed through standard ",[252,762,289],{}," -- you add the dependency just like any other Bun package.",[314,765,769],{"className":766,"code":767,"language":768,"meta":319,"style":319},"language-json shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","{\n    \"dependencies\": {\n        \"@my-org\u002Fdata\": \"workspace:*\"\n    }\n}\n","json",[252,770,771,776,790,810,814],{"__ignoreMap":319},[323,772,773],{"class":325,"line":326},[323,774,775],{"class":336},"{\n",[323,777,778,781,784,786,788],{"class":325,"line":360},[323,779,780],{"class":336},"    \"",[323,782,783],{"class":370},"dependencies",[323,785,404],{"class":336},[323,787,377],{"class":336},[323,789,386],{"class":336},[323,791,792,795,798,800,802,804,807],{"class":325,"line":367},[323,793,794],{"class":336},"        \"",[323,796,797],{"class":380},"@my-org\u002Fdata",[323,799,404],{"class":336},[323,801,377],{"class":336},[323,803,398],{"class":336},[323,805,806],{"class":353},"workspace:*",[323,808,809],{"class":336},"\"\n",[323,811,812],{"class":325,"line":389},[323,813,510],{"class":336},[323,815,816],{"class":325,"line":410},[323,817,552],{"class":336},[229,819,820],{},"When the application is deployed, the platform resolves these internal dependencies and ensures all projects are available to each other through the Service Directory.",[233,822,824],{"id":823},"deployable-packages","Deployable packages",[229,826,827,828,830],{},"When a push deploys a project (see ",[267,829,119],{"href":120},"), the\nplatform finds the packages it deploys by where they sit in the workspace:",[241,832,833,854],{},[244,834,835,838,839,842,843,845,846,849,850,853],{},[247,836,837],{},"Microservices"," live directly under ",[252,840,841],{},"packages\u002Fmicroservices",", one package each. A\nmicroservice runs in a VM of its own from its ",[252,844,289],{}," ",[252,847,848],{},"main",", or ",[252,851,852],{},"src\u002Fmain.ts"," when\nit declares none.",[244,855,856,838,859,862,863,866,867,870,871,873,874,876],{},[247,857,858],{},"UIs",[252,860,861],{},"packages\u002Fui",", one package each, and declare a ",[252,864,865],{},"build"," script\nthat writes ",[252,868,869],{},"dist\u002Findex.html",". A package under ",[252,872,861],{}," without a ",[252,875,865],{}," script is a\nlibrary and is left alone.",[229,878,879,880,845,882,884,885,888,889,892],{},"A package's identity is the unscoped part of its ",[252,881,289],{},[252,883,659],{}," (",[252,886,887],{},"@acme\u002Fadmin"," is\n",[252,890,891],{},"admin","), which must be lowercase letters, digits, and interior dashes and unique among the\npackages of its kind. The directory name never matters.",[296,894,896],{"id":895},"the-ui-build-contract","The UI build contract",[229,898,899,900,903,904,907],{},"Every UI is built during the deployment with ",[252,901,902],{},"bun run build",", and the build is handed the\nplatform's address as three variables. Vite exposes ",[252,905,906],{},"VITE_*"," variables to the page on its\nown, so a Vite project reads them with no configuration; a UI with another build tool must\npass them through itself:",[594,909,910,923],{},[597,911,912],{},[600,913,914,917,920],{},[603,915,916],{},"Variable",[603,918,919],{},"Value",[603,921,922],{},"What the UI does with it",[609,924,925,941,956],{},[600,926,927,932,938],{},[614,928,929],{},[252,930,931],{},"VITE_KINOTIC_HOST",[614,933,934,935],{},"e.g. ",[252,936,937],{},"api.kinotic.ai",[614,939,940],{},"The host the UI connects to Kinotic on from a browser",[600,942,943,948,953],{},[614,944,945],{},[252,946,947],{},"VITE_KINOTIC_PORT",[614,949,934,950],{},[252,951,952],{},"443",[614,954,955],{},"Its port",[600,957,958,963,970],{},[614,959,960],{},[252,961,962],{},"VITE_KINOTIC_USE_SSL",[614,964,965,583,967],{},[252,966,713],{},[252,968,969],{},"false",[614,971,972],{},"Whether to connect over TLS",[314,974,976],{"className":316,"code":975,"language":318,"meta":319,"style":319},"await Kinotic.connect({\n    server: {\n        host: import.meta.env.VITE_KINOTIC_HOST,\n        port: parseInt(import.meta.env.VITE_KINOTIC_PORT),\n        useSSL: import.meta.env.VITE_KINOTIC_USE_SSL === 'true',\n    },\n})\n",[252,977,978,997,1006,1032,1061,1095,1100],{"__ignoreMap":319},[323,979,980,983,986,988,992,995],{"class":325,"line":326},[323,981,982],{"class":329},"await",[323,984,985],{"class":340}," Kinotic",[323,987,270],{"class":336},[323,989,991],{"class":990},"s2Zo4","connect",[323,993,994],{"class":340},"(",[323,996,775],{"class":336},[323,998,999,1002,1004],{"class":325,"line":360},[323,1000,1001],{"class":392},"    server",[323,1003,377],{"class":336},[323,1005,386],{"class":336},[323,1007,1008,1011,1013,1016,1018,1021,1023,1026,1028,1030],{"class":325,"line":367},[323,1009,1010],{"class":392},"        host",[323,1012,377],{"class":336},[323,1014,1015],{"class":329}," import",[323,1017,270],{"class":336},[323,1019,1020],{"class":340},"meta",[323,1022,270],{"class":336},[323,1024,1025],{"class":340},"env",[323,1027,270],{"class":336},[323,1029,931],{"class":340},[323,1031,407],{"class":336},[323,1033,1034,1037,1039,1042,1044,1046,1048,1050,1052,1054,1056,1059],{"class":325,"line":389},[323,1035,1036],{"class":392},"        port",[323,1038,377],{"class":336},[323,1040,1041],{"class":990}," parseInt",[323,1043,994],{"class":340},[323,1045,330],{"class":329},[323,1047,270],{"class":336},[323,1049,1020],{"class":340},[323,1051,270],{"class":336},[323,1053,1025],{"class":340},[323,1055,270],{"class":336},[323,1057,1058],{"class":340},"VITE_KINOTIC_PORT)",[323,1060,407],{"class":336},[323,1062,1063,1066,1068,1070,1072,1074,1076,1078,1080,1083,1086,1088,1090,1093],{"class":325,"line":410},[323,1064,1065],{"class":392},"        useSSL",[323,1067,377],{"class":336},[323,1069,1015],{"class":329},[323,1071,270],{"class":336},[323,1073,1020],{"class":340},[323,1075,270],{"class":336},[323,1077,1025],{"class":340},[323,1079,270],{"class":336},[323,1081,1082],{"class":340},"VITE_KINOTIC_USE_SSL ",[323,1084,1085],{"class":336},"===",[323,1087,350],{"class":336},[323,1089,713],{"class":353},[323,1091,1092],{"class":336},"'",[323,1094,407],{"class":336},[323,1096,1097],{"class":325,"line":427},[323,1098,1099],{"class":336},"    },\n",[323,1101,1102,1105],{"class":325,"line":444},[323,1103,1104],{"class":336},"}",[323,1106,1107],{"class":340},")\n",[229,1109,1110,1111,1113],{},"A build that does not write ",[252,1112,869],{}," fails the deployment naming the UI.",[229,1115,1116,1119,1120,1123,1124,1127,1128,1131,1132,1135],{},[252,1117,1118],{},"dist"," is published as it is, from the site's root: files under ",[252,1121,1122],{},"assets\u002F"," carry a content\nhash in their name and are cached for a year, everything else is never cached. Each site\nalso publishes the commit it serves as ",[252,1125,1126],{},"version.json"," next to its ",[252,1129,1130],{},"index.html",", never\ncached, as ",[252,1133,1134],{},"{ \"commitSha\": \"\u003Ccommit>\" }",". A publish replaces the previous commit's files;\na tab left open on the previous commit loads the new commit when it next reloads.",[233,1137,1139],{"id":1138},"typical-setup","Typical Setup",[229,1141,1142,1143,1146,1147,1149,1150,1152,1153,1155],{},"Most applications start with a single project created through Kinotic OS, which provisions a GitHub repository scaffolded as a Bun workspace mono repo: ",[252,1144,1145],{},"packages\u002Fdomain"," (entity model and generated repositories), ",[252,1148,841],{},", ",[252,1151,861],{},", and a ",[252,1154,293],{}," wired to the owning organization and application. Clone the provisioned repository and start building.",[229,1157,1158,1159,1161],{},"As the application grows, you can add additional projects for microservices, batch jobs, or frontends -- each with its own ",[252,1160,293],{}," pointing to the same application identifier.",[1163,1164,1165],"style",{},"html pre.shiki code .s7zQu, html code.shiki .s7zQu{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-light-font-style:italic;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-default-font-style:italic;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark-font-style:italic}html pre.shiki code .sMK4o, html code.shiki .sMK4o{--shiki-light:#39ADB5;--shiki-default:#89DDFF;--shiki-dark:#89DDFF}html pre.shiki code .sTEyZ, html code.shiki .sTEyZ{--shiki-light:#90A4AE;--shiki-default:#EEFFFF;--shiki-dark:#BABED8}html pre.shiki code .sfazB, html code.shiki .sfazB{--shiki-light:#91B859;--shiki-default:#C3E88D;--shiki-dark:#C3E88D}html pre.shiki code .spNyl, html code.shiki .spNyl{--shiki-light:#9